# SUMMARIZE, ELTS, ECHO, STATUS and RESET on the manual's Cassegrain (cmdref: Session & Files).  NONE sets
# the plot type to NULL and OBS ALL the obscuration option to 0; RESET returns the obscuration option to 1
# (POSITIVE) and, since PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (i) (2026-10-22), the plot type to its start-up GRAY (it left
# NULL in force before: red on the pre-fix binary).  The prescription stays loaded across RESET.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
summarize
elts
echo marker line for the journal
none
obs
all
status
reset
status
# EXPECT: Optical Train Summary:\s+Tracing rays past\s+5 elements
# EXPECT: Element name = Primary\s+ID =\s+2
# EXPECT: Element name = Detector\s+ID =\s+5
# EXPECT: ^marker line for the journal
# EXPECT: Obscuration option for ray-trace=\s+0\s+Current WF plot type=NULL[\s\S]*?MACOS> reset[\s\S]*?Obscuration option for ray-trace=\s+1\s+Current WF plot type=GRAY
# EXPECT-NOT: Must load optical data first
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
